.TH TULPAR-HOLD 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.1.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-hold \- block a package from upgrade or removal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar hold
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar g
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar \-g
.RI [ options "] " name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Marks an installed package as held. Held packages are blocked from
upgrade and removal until released with
.BR tulpar-unhold (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate on an alternate root instead of the live system.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the package is not installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-unhold (1)
